    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 8,
    "title": "Ask about manner and emphasize a claim",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-rhetorical-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Ask about manner and emphasize a claim",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "不是…吗 can remind the listener of something the speaker believes is already agreed or known. In this context it challenges a misunderstanding, rather than neutrally asking for new information. 怎样 + verb can ask a genuine method question or, with an impossible situation made explicit, challenge how the action could be possible.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "不是说明天来吗？",
                "pinyin": "bù shì shuō míngtiān lái ma ？",
                "meaning": "Did you not say you would come tomorrow?",
                "audio": "fd0193d93f01828711c1a84288ca253aea260ee103839294d350d6009ab56891"
              },
              {
                "text": "没有书，我们怎样学习？",
                "pinyin": "méiyǒu shū ， wǒmen zěnyàng xuéxí ？",
                "meaning": "With no books, how are we supposed to study? A rhetorical challenge in this context.",
                "audio": "eeddfdce896600aaaa1e07b165a38e8ac2e957a9d72cb3c571ba89f2f49852f4"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
